&lt;!-- Abilities --&gt;
&lt;div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"&gt;
    @@foreach (var ability in selectedPokemon.Abilities)
    {
        &lt;span class="px-3 py-1 bg-green-100 text-green-700 
                     rounded-full text-sm capitalize"&gt;
            @@ability.Ability.Name
        &lt;/span&gt;
    }
&lt;/div&gt;</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Important Notes & Tips (White Card) -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-200 mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">📝 Important Notes & Tips</h2>

            <div class="space-y-3">
                <!-- Pro Tips (Blue) -->
                <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-lg p-4">
                    <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-blue-900 mb-3">💡 Pro Tips</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-4">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-2">Use @@bind:after for automatic
                                pagination reset</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-blue-800">Instead of manually calling pagination logic in every event
                                handler, let <code>@@bind:after</code> do it automatically! Whenever the search changes,
                                your <code>OnSearchChanged()</code> method runs and resets the page. Clean and
                                automatic!</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-2">Always use
                                StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase for search</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-blue-800">Users don't want to worry about capitalization. Using
                                <code>OrdinalIgnoreCase</code> means "pika", "Pika", "PIKA" all work. It's a small
                                detail that makes your search feel way more flexible and user-friendly!
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-2">stopPropagation prevents click events
                                from bubbling up</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-blue-800">When you click the modal content, that click would normally
                                bubble up to the overlay and close the modal. <code>@@onclick:stopPropagation</code>
                                stops that! The click stays on the content and doesn't reach the overlay.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-2">Remember to divide height and weight by
                                10</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-blue-800">The PokeAPI returns height in decimeters and weight in
                                hectograms (weird, right?). Just divide both by 10.0 to convert to meters and kilograms.
                                Much easier for people to understand!</p>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-2">Show a "Found X Pokemon" count for
                                search feedback</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-blue-800">When users search, they want to know how many results
                                matched. Display <code>FilteredPokemon.Count</code> below the search box so they can see
                                if their search is working or if they need to try different terms.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Troubleshooting (Yellow) -->
                <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 rounded-lg p-4">
                    <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-yellow-900 mb-2">⚠️ Troubleshooting</h3>
                    <ul class="list-disc ml-6 text-sm text-yellow-900 space-y-1">
                        <li><strong>Search doesn't find results:</strong> Double-check you're using
                            <code>StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase</code>. Without it, "pikachu" won't match "Pikachu"
                            and your search won't work right.
                        </li>
                        <li><strong>Stuck on a blank page after searching:</strong> You forgot to reset the page number!
                            Add <code>@@bind:after="OnSearchChanged"</code> to your search input, and inside that method
                            set <code>currentPage = 1</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Modal closes when I click inside it:</strong> You need
                            <code>@@onclick:stopPropagation</code> on the modal content div. The overlay has
                            <code>@@onclick="CloseModal"</code>, but the content should stop that event from bubbling
                            up.
                        </li>
                        <li><strong>Can't close the modal:</strong> Make sure your <code>CloseModal()</code> method sets
                            <code>selectedPokemon = null</code>, and the modal only renders when
                            <code>selectedPokemon != null</code>.
                        </li>
                        <li><strong>Types and abilities don't show up:</strong> Check the nested structure! It's
                            <code>type.Type.Name</code> and <code>ability.Ability.Name</code> (capital T and A). The API
                            returns nested objects, not just strings.
                        </li>
                        <li><strong>Search only updates when I press Enter:</strong> Add
                            <code>@@bind:event="oninput"</code> to make it update with every keystroke instead of
                            waiting for the default <code>onchange</code> behavior (which fires on blur).
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- How to do it (Gradient Banner) -->
        <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-gray-100 to-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">🛠️ How to do it</h2>
            <ol class="list-decimal ml-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm sm:text-base">
                <li>
                    <strong>Create your component:</strong>
                    Make a new file called <code>Search.razor</code> in your <code>Components/Pages/Pokemon</code>
                    folder
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Add the search box:</strong>
                    Create an input with
                    <code>@@bind="searchQuery" @@bind:event="oninput" @@bind:after="OnSearchChanged"</code>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Filter the Pokemon list:</strong>
                    Use <code>Where(p => p.Name.Contains(searchQuery, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))</code>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Reset pagination when search changes:</strong>
                    In <code>OnSearchChanged()</code>, set <code>currentPage = 1</code> and recalculate
                    <code>totalPages</code>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Make cards clickable:</strong>
                    Add <code>@@onclick="@@(() => ShowDetails(id))"</code> to each Pokemon card
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Fetch detailed info:</strong>
                    In <code>ShowDetails()</code>, call <code>https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/pokemon/{id}</code>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Build the modal overlay:</strong>
                    Use <code>fixed inset-0 bg-black/50</code> with <code>@@onclick="CloseModal"</code>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Add the modal content:</strong>
                    Put <code>@@onclick:stopPropagation</code> on the white card so it doesn't close when clicked
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Show the details:</strong>
                    Display name, sprite, height÷10, weight÷10, types, and abilities
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Test it out:</strong>
                    Run your app, search for "char" or "pika", and click cards to see the magic happen!
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- Live Demo -->
        <div class="bg-black/3 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">🎬 Live Demo</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">Try it out! Type in the search box to filter Pokemon, then click any
                card to see a popup with detailed stats, types, and abilities. Notice how pagination automatically
                resets when you search!</p>

            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-6">
                <!-- Search input -->
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <input type="text" @bind="searchQuery" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:after="OnSearchChanged"
                        placeholder="Search Pokemon by name..." class="w-full px-4 py-2 border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-lg
                                  focus:border-blue-400 focus:outline-none" />

                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-2">
                        Found @FilteredPokemon.Count Pokemon
                    </p>
                </div>

                @if (isLoading)
                {
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-center p-12">
                        <div class="animate-spin rounded-full h-12 w-12 border-4 border-blue-600 border-t-transparent">
                        </div>
                        <span class="ml-3 text-gray-600">Loading Pokemon...</span>
                    </div>
                }
                else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(errorMessage))
                {
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border-2 border-red-200 rounded-xl p-6">
                        <p class="text-red-700">@errorMessage</p>
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <!-- Pokemon grid -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-4">
                        @foreach (var pokemon in CurrentPagePokemon)
                        {
                            int id = GetPokemonId(pokemon.Url);

                            <div @onclick="@(async () => await ShowDetails(id))"
                                class="border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden 
                                                                                                                                        hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xl 
                                                                                                                                        transition-all duration-200 cursor-pointer">

                                <div class="aspect-square bg-linear-to-br from-gray-50 to-gray-100">
                                    <img src="@GetSpriteUrl(id)"
                                        class="w-full h-full object-contain p-2
                                                                                                                                                hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300"
                                        alt="@pokemon.Name" loading="lazy" />
                                </div>

                                <div class="p-3 bg-white">
                                    <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 font-mono">
                                        #@id.ToString("D3")
                                    </span>
                                    <p
                                        class="font-semibold text-gray-800 capitalize 
                                                                                                                                              hover:text-blue-600 transition-colors">
                                        @pokemon.Name
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>

                    <!-- Pagination -->
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between mt-6">
                        <button @onclick="PreviousPage" disabled="@(currentPage == 1)"
                            class="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-lg
                                                                                       hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors
                                                                                       disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed">
                            ← Previous
                        </button>

                        <span class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                            Page @currentPage of @totalPages
                        </span>

                        <button @onclick="NextPage" disabled="@(currentPage >= totalPages)"
                            class="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-lg
                                                                                       hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors
                                                                                       disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed">
                            Next →
                        </button>
                    </div>
                }
            </div>

            <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-4 text-center">💡 Try searching for "char" or "pika" and click Pokemon to
                see details!</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Modal for Pokemon details -->
        @if (selectedPokemon != null)
        {
            <div @onclick="CloseModal" class="fixed inset-0 bg-black/50 flex items-center justify-center z-50 p-4">

                <div @onclick:stopPropagation class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-2xl p-6 max-w-md w-full">

                    <!-- Close button -->
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold capitalize">@selectedPokemon.Name</h2>
                        <button @onclick="CloseModal" class="text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-700 text-2xl">
                            ✕
                        </button>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Pokemon sprite -->
                    <img src="@GetSpriteUrl(selectedPokemon.Id)" class="w-48 h-48 mx-auto" alt="@selectedPokemon.Name" />

                    <!-- Stats -->
                    <div class="mt-4 space-y-2">
                        <p class="text-sm">
                            <strong>Height:</strong> @(selectedPokemon.Height / 10.0)m
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-sm">
                            <strong>Weight:</strong> @(selectedPokemon.Weight / 10.0)kg
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-sm">
                            <strong>Base Experience:</strong> @selectedPokemon.Base_Experience
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Types -->
                    <div class="mt-4">
                        <p class="text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Types:</p>
                        <div class="flex gap-2">
                            @foreach (var type in selectedPokemon.Types)
                            {
                                <span
                                    class="px-3 py-1 bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 
                                                                                                                                             rounded-full text-sm capitalize">
                                    @type.Type.Name
                                </span>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Abilities -->
                    <div class="mt-4">
                        <p class="text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Abilities:</p>
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                            @foreach (var ability in selectedPokemon.Abilities)
                            {
                                <span
                                    class="px-3 py-1 bg-green-100 text-green-700 
                                                                                                                                             rounded-full text-sm capitalize">
                                    @ability.Ability.Name
                                </span>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Close button -->
                    <button @onclick="CloseModal"
                        class="w-full mt-6 px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 
                                                                                   text-white rounded-lg transition-colors">
                        Close
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>
        }

        <!-- Mark Complete (Green Card) -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border-2 border-green-200 mb-6">
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4">
                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Finished Step 6?</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Awesome progress! Keep going! 🚀</p>
                </div>
                @if (isComplete)
                {
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                        <span class="px-4 py-2 rounded-full bg-green-100 text-green-700 font-medium">✓ Completed</span>
                        <button @onclick="ResetStep"
                            class="px-4 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors text-sm">Reset</button>
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <button @onclick="MarkComplete"
                        class="px-6 py-3 bg-green-600 hover:bg-green-700 text-white rounded-lg font-medium transition-colors">Mark
                        as Complete</button>
                }
            </div>
        </div>



        <!-- Navigation -->
        <div class="mt-8">
            <div class="bg-black/90 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 text-white text-center">
                <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Great work! 🎉</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-300 mb-6 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
                    You've learned search, filtering, and modals! Next, Step 7 will show you how to build the complete,
                    polished Pokedex demo with type filtering, evolution chains, and beautiful visualizations!
                </p>
                <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-3">
                    <a href="/pokemon-guide"
                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 rounded-xl transition-colors">
                        <span class="text-lg">←</span>
                        <span class="text-sm sm:text-base font-semibold">Back to Guide</span>
                    </a>
                    <a href="/pokemon-examples/step5"
                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 rounded-xl transition-colors">
                        <span class="text-lg">←</span>
                        <span class="text-sm sm:text-base font-semibold">Previous: Step 5</span>
                    </a>
                    <a href="/pokemon-examples/step7"
                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 rounded-xl transition-colors">
                        <span class="text-sm sm:text-base font-semibold">Next: Step 7</span>
                        <span class="text-lg">→</span>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>